"""Deli Counter 0.252.0 (the factory's roadmap 284): a piece that seats somebody stands with its chair.

51 of 255 dining tables, 41 of 263 desks and 4 of 46 cocktail tables stood with no chair. A host the room left
chairless is seated last, when the room is furnished, so nothing else furnish drew there moves: one chair from its own
stream, tucked then pushed in, off any reserved route; a host no chair fits beside goes. 77 rooms of 55 specs
refurnished and sheltered.

What this writes, every target pinned by its hash and refused on a mismatch, nothing written until every file has been
worked out: `level_design.py` and `test_marker_room_routes.py` (anchored hunks); the fifty-five refurnished specs,
carried whole; the new `test_seated_hosts.py`; VERSION; the CHANGELOG entry, prepended. Generated from a proven clone
(`patches/dc_table_chairs/gen_dc_table_chairs.py`), dry-run on a fresh clone to the clone's every byte, a second run
refused (`patches/dc_table_chairs/dry_run_*.out.txt`).

    python patches/patch_dc_table_chairs.py
    cd deli_counter && python build.py --all && python -m pytest -q && python check.py
"""
